"hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:"
530,"Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:""It is from the SUnnah to leave for the Eid walking"
531,"**Narrated by Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him):**

The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), Abu Bakr, and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to perform the prayer of the two 'Eids before the sermon (khutbah), after which they would deliver the sermon.

**It is also reported in this chapter from Jabir and Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them).**

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Ibn 'Umar is a *hasan sahih* (good and authentic) hadith. The established practice (*'amal*) among the scholars from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others is that the prayer of the two 'Eids precedes the sermon. It is also said that the first person to deliver the sermon before the prayer was Marwan ibn al-Hakam."
532,"Jabir bin Samurah narrated:""I prayed the two Eid prayers with the Prophet - not one time"
533,"Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir: ""The Prophet (ﷺ) used to recite in the two 'Eids and in Jumu'ah: 'Sabbih Isma Rabbika Al-A'la' and 'Hal Ataka Hadith Al-Ghashiyah,' and sometimes they would fall on the same day, so he would recite them both.""

[Abu 'Eisa said:] There are other narrations on this topic from Abu Waqid, Samurah bin Jundab, and Ibn 'Abbas.

Abu 'Eisa said: The Hadith of An-Nu'man bin Bashir is Hasan Sahih. This is how Sufyan Ath-Thawri and Mis'ar reported it from Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, similar to the narration of Abu 'Awanah. As for Sufyan bin 'Uyainah, there is a difference in the narration from him; it is reported from him from Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib bin Salim, from his father, from An-Nu'man bin Bashir. But we do not know of Habib bin Salim narrating from his father. Habib bin Salim was the freed slave of An-Nu'man bin Bashir, and he narrated several Hadiths from An-Nu'man bin Bashir. It has also been reported from Ibn 'Uyainah, from Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, in a manner similar to the narration of these (other narrators). It has been reported that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to recite in the prayer of the two 'Eids: ""Iqtarabat As-Sa'ah,"" and this is what Ash-Shafi'i says."
534,"Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah narrated:""Umar bin Al-Khattab asked Abu Waqid Al-Laithi what Allah's Messenger would recite during Al-Fitr and Al-Adha"
535,"Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah:There is a another chain with similar narration"
536,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Muslim ibn 'Amr Abu 'Amr al-Hadda' al-Madani narrated to us:** 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh narrated to us, from Kathir ibn 'Abdullah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ performed *takbir* on the two 'Eids: in the first *rak'ah* he made seven *takbirs* before the recitation, and in the second *rak'ah* he made five *takbirs* before the recitation.

He said: And in this chapter there are narrations from 'A'isha, Ibn 'Umar, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr.

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Kathir's grandfather is a *hasan* hadith, and it is the best thing narrated in this chapter from the Prophet ﷺ. His name is 'Amr ibn 'Auf al-Muzani.

And this is the practice upon which some of the people of knowledge acted, from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others. And it is narrated similarly from Abu Hurayra that he prayed in Madinah in a manner close to this prayer, and this is the position of the people of Madinah. Upon this say Malik ibn Anas, al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq.

It is narrated that 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said regarding the *takbir* on the two 'Eids: in the first *rak'ah* there are five *takbirs* before the recitation, and in the second *rak'ah* one begins with the recitation, then performs four *takbirs* along with the *takbir* of *ruku'*. And something similar to this has been narrated from more than one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and this is the position of the people of Kufa. Upon this says Sufyan al-Thawri."
537,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet went out on the day of Al-Fitr"
538,"Abu Bakr bin Hafs - and he is Ibn Umar bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqas - narrated about Ibn Umar"
539,"Umm Atiyyah narrated:""Allah's Messenger would order the virgins"
540,"There is a similar narration from Umm Atiyyah :with another chain"
541,"Abu Hurairah narrated:""When Allah's Messenger would go out on the day of Eid by one route"
542,"Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father:""The Prophet would not leave on the Day of Fitr until he ate"
543,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Prophet would have a breakfast of dates on the Day of Fitr before leaving for the Musalla"
